# Proton GE (arm64) — a SECOND compat tool alongside proton-cachyos, both of which run x86/x86-64
# *Windows* games on this device. GloriousEggroll's GE-Proton and CachyOS's proton-cachyos are two
# community Proton builds of the SAME shape: an arm64-native Wine plus Valve's WoW64 FEX
# (files/lib/wine/aarch64-windows/libwow64fex.dll, libarm64ecfex.dll). The emulator translates only
# the game's x86 Windows code; every Linux syscall is made by the arm64 side of Wine. So this path
# is SELF-CONTAINED: no system FEX package, no x86 guest rootfs, no thunks, no Steam Linux Runtime.
#
# We ship BOTH so the user can pick whichever runs a given title better from the Steam UI — GE and
# CachyOS carry different game fixes, Wine bases, and DXVK/vkd3d snapshots. Everything the CachyOS
# pin documents about *why we bake a Proton at all* (require_tool_appid gating on a non-Deckard
# client; nothing downloadable before first-boot Wi-Fi/OOBE) applies identically here — see
# packages/proton-cachyos/prebuilt.pin for that reasoning.
#
# Like CachyOS, this tarball's own toolmanifest.vdf carries `require_tool_appid` and its
# compatibilitytool.vdf uses the dated build string as the internal name. assemble-rootfs.sh's
# shared rewrite_proton_tool rewrites BOTH tools the same way after extraction (drops require_tool,
# fronts our FEX wrapper, pins a stable internal name + friendly display_name). Do not "fix" the
# manifest here; the tarball is upstream content and is extracted verbatim.
#
# strip: 1 + dest: the archive is rooted at the versioned directory (GE-Proton11-6-aarch64/), so
# stripping that component lands its CONTENTS directly in a stable, version-free directory name.
# NOTE the directory name is cosmetic: Steam pins a game to the tool's INTERNAL name (the
# compat_tools key inside compatibilitytool.vdf), not the directory — so assemble-rootfs.sh also
# rewrites that internal name to a stable id (proton-ge-arm64), or a GE minor bump (GE-Proton11-1 ->
# GE-Proton11-2) would unpin every game. See rewrite_proton_tool in assemble-rootfs.sh.
#
# The tool lives under /usr/share/steam/compatibilitytools.d, which the client does NOT scan on its
# own — novadeck-steam adds it via STEAM_EXTRA_COMPAT_TOOLS_PATHS (the whole dir, so both tools are
# picked up). So it needs no seeding into $HOME and is replaced atomically with the OS slot.
#
# Upstream publishes a .sha512sum sidecar; the sha256 below was computed from the artifact.
#
# Fields: see packages/inputplumber/prebuilt.pin, plus `dest` (extraction root) documented in
# packages/fex-rootfs/prebuilt.pin.
#
# To bump: pick a release from https://github.com/GloriousEggroll/proton-ge-custom/releases carrying
# an `-aarch64.tar.gz` asset, set version + url + sha256 together, and keep `dest` unchanged so games
# stay pinned to the same tool name. Re-verify the version parse in assemble-rootfs.sh's GE block
# still matches (it fails loudly if upstream changes the `version` file format).
name: proton-ge
version: GE-Proton11-6
url: https://github.com/GloriousEggroll/proton-ge-custom/releases/download/GE-Proton11-6/GE-Proton11-6-aarch64.tar.gz
sha256: 77929dcd5f951b1a1b89fe594d91878a3adf9516406f68076971988ee2cfdf43
kind: tar
strip: 1
dest: /usr/share/steam/compatibilitytools.d/proton-ge-arm64
# `proton` is a python3 script (#!/usr/bin/env python3); the wrapper that fronts it is python too.
deps: python
